- - -
@section tel_resp Telephony APIs Response handling
- - -

The framework allows responses to each API to be configured using a JSON file.<br>
Each manager has its own JSON configuration file present under <i>simulation/json/api/tel/</i> <br>

Example for API command response for telux::tel::ISmsManager::SendSms<br>
<pre>
"SendSms" :
    [
        {   "numberOfSegments" : 2,
            "status" : "SUCCESS"
        },
        {
            "smsResponseCbErrorCode" : "SUCCESS",
            "smsResponseCbDelay" : 9000,
            "smsResponseCbMsgRefs" : "1 2"
        },
        {
            "onDeliveryReportErrorCode" : "SUCCESS",
            "onDeliveryReportMsgRef" : 1,
            "onDeliveryReportCallbackDelay" : 12000
        },
        {
            "onDeliveryReportErrorCode" : "SUCCESS",
            "onDeliveryReportMsgRef" : 2,
            "onDeliveryReportCallbackDelay" : 12000
        }
    ]
</pre>
Here, clients are expected to provide the inputs for JSON attributes of API according to an encoded message.
<br>
The table explains the configuration for API response parameters of <i>simulation/json/api/tel/ISmsManagerSlot*.json</i>.
@table{2,{\raggedright}p{2.00in},{\raggedright}p{4.80in}}
@trfirsthdg
@thmultcol{1,|c|} Json Attribute @thmultcolend @thmultcollast{1,c|} Description @thmultcollastend
@trfirsthdgend
@trhdg
@thdg{1,|c|,Json Attribute} @thdglast{1,c|,Description}
@trhdgend

@tr @td numberOfSegments @tdend @tdlast Signifies number of segments present in encoded message. @tdlastend @trend
@tr @td status @tdend @tdlast Status of request. @tdlastend @trend
@tr @td sentCallbackErrorCode, smsResponseCbErrorCode @tdend @tdlast Response callback errorcode. @tdlastend @trend
@tr @td sentCallbackDelay, smsResponseCbDelay @tdend @tdlast Response callback delay. @tdlastend @trend
@tr @td sentCallbackMsgRefs, smsResponseCbMsgRefs @tdend @tdlast Add reference number for every message segment according to numberOfSegments with one space between the digits. @tdlastend @trend
@tr @td deliveryCallbackErrorCode @tdend @tdlast Delivery report for individual segment is invoked using delivery callback error @tdlastend @trend
@tr @td deliveryCallbackDelay, onDeliveryReportCallbackDelay @tdend @tdlast Delivery report for individual segment is invoked using delivery callback delay. @tdlastend @trend
@tr @td onDeliveryReportErrorCode @tdend @tdlast Delivery callback errorcode. @tdlastend @trend
@tr @td onDeliveryReportMsgRef @tdend @tdlast Delivery report for message reference of a segment. @tdlastend @trend
@tr @td receiverAddress @tdend @tdlast Input receiver address according to encoded pdu. @tdlastend @trend

@tableend

<br>
- - -
@section tel_states Telephony data handling
- - -

@subsection tel_dataCard Card

Details of parameters currently configured in the Simulation framework to perform pin operations. <br>

- "Pin1password" : "1234"  - Password for PIN1 operations for public APIs changeCardPassword, unlockCardByPin, changeCardPassword.<br>
- "Pin2password" : "5678" - Password for PIN2 operations for public API changeCardPassword, unlockCardByPin, changeCardPassword.<br>
- "Puk1password" : 11111111 - Password for puk1 for public API unlockCardByPuk.<br>
- "Puk2password" : 22222222 - Password for puk2 for public API unlockCardByPuk.<br>

file: <i>simulation/json/system-state/tel/ICardManagerStateSlot*.json</i> <br>

@subsubsection tel_cardfiles Details of supported apps, EF files, and records


All the EF files are considered to be present at same file structure directory of simulated SIM files.<br>
User input for filepaths provided using APIs present under telux::tel::ICardFileHandler is not validated in the simulation library.<br>
<h3>ADF files</h1>
